' bug-464 byte-identity codegen-coverage fixture (compile-only, never executed).
'
' This exists for the targets this machine cannot RUN. The live-slot transfer
' copy is per-backend by construction -- a `tls::Socket`'s record tail is
' `SSL_CTX*`@32 + `SSL*`@40 on OpenSSL, an ARENA SSPI block@40 on Schannel (which
' must be deep-copied, not aliased), and ctx@32 + queue@40 on Network.framework.
' The macOS path is proven at runtime by
' `tests/rt-behavior/threads/thread-transfer-tls-socket-rt`, but no test on this
' host ever executes the OpenSSL or Schannel forms, and no Windows binary is run
' by any test at all.
'
' A byte-identity fixture is the available substitute: it is lowered for EVERY
' registered target by `builtin_codegen_corpora_lower_in_process` and pinned by
' five per-target `.ncodesum` goldens. That does not prove the Schannel deep-copy
' is CORRECT -- only that it is emitted, and that it does not silently change
' afterwards. The distinction is recorded in bug-464's STATUS block; do not read
' a green gate here as runtime proof on Windows or Linux.
'
' Compile-only, so `tls::connect` never has to reach a peer.
IMPORT tls
IMPORT thread
IMPORT xfer_tls_worker

FUNC main AS Integer
  LET t AS Thread OF RES tls::Socket TO Boolean = thread::start(xfer_tls_worker::talkOnTransferredSocket, "dns.google")
  RES conn = tls::connect("8.8.8.8", 443, 30000, "dns.google")
  ' The call that emits `copy_resource_to_current_arena` for a resource WITH
  ' declared live slots -- the whole point of the fixture.
  thread::transfer(t, conn)
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
